     "identifier": "KS-1926",
     "title": "package_format_gate.test.sh picks its \"dead\" pid with kill -0 (cases 20 and 32), so a live process owned by another user fails the push at random",
     "state": {
      "name": "Backlog"
     },
     "description": "**BLUF:** the shell-suite cell \"a stage of a DEAD pid is swept\" in `systemTest/__tests__/package_format_gate.test.sh` (case 20, check at line 662) fails at random on macOS, and a failed shell suite makes pre-push leg 14 refuse the push. The test picks its \"dead\" pid with `kill -0`, which reports failure (EPERM) for a live process owned by another user; the gate under test decides with `ps -p`, sees that process alive and correctly leaves the stage. The gate is right and the test's pid pick is wrong. Found 2026-11-01 when a push of an unrelated change was refused on exactly this cell. Priority Low: the chance per run is small, but it lands on any push, whoever makes it.\n\n## Where\n\n* The test draws the pid at line 654: `dead=$((50000 + RANDOM % 9000)); while kill -0 \"$dead\" 2>/dev/null; do dead=$((dead + 1)); done`. The same line is at 883 (case 32, \"the tree dir is cleaned up, killed or not, and a dead run's is swept\"). Only case 20's draw was read closely; case 32 uses the identical expression and the same gate function.\n* The gate: `systemTest/scripts/check-package-format.sh` lines 319-337 (`_sweep_dead_stages`). Its own comment says: `ps -p` rather than `kill -0`: the latter reports EPERM, i.e. \"failed\", for a live process owned by someone else.\n\n## How it fails\n\nWhen the random draw lands on a live process owned by another user (root daemons, another account), the test treats it as dead, plants a stage directory for that pid, runs the gate, and finds the stage still there: `FAIL a stage of a DEAD pid is swept` with `want \"no\", got \"yes\"`. The chance per run is (live other-user pids in 50000 to 58999) / 9000. Measured on 2026-11-01 on one Mac: 19 such pids of 9000 (about 0.2%; root plus one other account). It varies with the machine and the day.\n\n## Reproduction (deterministic)\n\nA scratch copy holding the shared helpers (lines 1-258) and case 20 only, with the random pick replaced by a fixed pid, run on develop `d7691f35312e`:\n\n* pid 54986, a live root process (`ps -p` rc 0, `kill -0` rc 1): `FAIL a stage of a DEAD pid is swept`, `want \"no\", got \"yes\"`, 7 passed and 1 failed.\n* pid 50500, free (both rc 1): 8 passed, 0 failed.\n  The scratch scripts and both outputs are in the seat folder of the session that found it: `5_Project_History/2026-11-01_seatR-71st/evidence/pr1/pkgfmt/` (`zz_r71_repro_live.test.sh`, `zz_r71_repro_free.test.sh`, `repro_live.out`, `repro_free.out`). No repository file was touched.\n\n## Observed in\n\nA push of a demo-service change (head `3a88693f70d3` on develop `d7691f35312e`), 2026-11-01 11:11Z: leg 14 shell suites 105 passed, 1 failed, 1 skipped; this cell was the only red of 434 in this file. The failure is unrelated to that change.\n\n## Fix shape (not made here: the test is outside the filing session's partition)\n\nPick the pid the way the gate decides, with `ps -p`: `while ps -p \"$dead\" >/dev/null 2>&1; do dead=$((dead + 1)); done`, at both lines.\n\n## Related and board search\n\nKS 1611 (Backlog) covers five other intermittent cells in this file (real npm) and does not name this one. Searched (issue text and comments): `package_format_gate` 5 hits (KS 998, KS 1583, KS 1605, KS 1611, KS 1716); `stage of a DEAD pid` 0; `format-gate-stage` 0; `EPERM` 0; `kill -0` 1 (KS 1324, a different test); `dead pid` 1 (KS 912, a different test). No ticket both concerns this gate or test and mentions `kill -0` or a dead pid. Positive control: the file-name token finds KS 1611. Random-token control: 0 hits.\n\n## Not known\n\nWhether the second draw (line 883) has been seen to fail; how often pushes were refused on this cell before 2026-11-01 (no earlier record found by the searches above).",
     "comments": {
      "nodes": []
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 }
